A. Commit message:
Move coredump registration to the worker thread for older version compatibility

B. Change summary:
The patch moves the coredump registration from the initial capture call to the worker thread to ensure safe memory allocation using arbitrary GFP flags. Additionally, it addresses changes in included headers and function signatures to maintain compatibility with the older version.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Medium: Code diff will be applied and a pull request will be sent to the developer to merge, but there are no indirect changes expected to be done in other parts of the system.

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
